<urn:atm:triage:finding/AZS4-QA-009>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AZS4-QA-009" ;
  triage:title "Positional-tuple swap risk in attention-scheduler code (RBP-F002)" ;
  triage:description "CORRECTED 2026-09-10T15:49:00Z: the original triage pass mis-scoped this to attention_schedule_store.rs:398 (item_columns()) -- a real but different, unfiled rust-best-practices-agent 'out-of-scope observation', not RBP-F002. quality-mgr independently confirmed the actual RBP-F002 site is crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/ops.rs:28, the DecomposedWorkflowColumns type alias: an 8-field positional tuple (6x Option<&str>, 2x trailing Option<String>) with 3 same-shaped Option<&str> fields that could be silently swapped without a compiler error. Cipher's fix at attention_schedule_store.rs (item_columns -> named ItemColumns struct, commit 6a09f7a54) is a legitimate improvement but does not close this finding -- writer/ops.rs:28 is still unchanged." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
